### PYTHON & ENVIRONMENT
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
.env

### DATA & OUTPUTS (The 2.6GB+ Culprits)
# Ignore all CSV and PNG files because these are your MC outputs/plots.
# These are the actual bulk -- regenerate them by re-running the models.
*.csv
*.png

# NO DATA FILES IN GITHUB.               decided 2026-08-13
#
# The whole Data/ tree is untracked -- inputs, deliverables and third-party
# source material alike. Nothing under Data/ goes to the remote.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE CLONING. A fresh clone gets the CODE ONLY and cannot run:
# every model reads its assumptions from Data/*.xlsx, so without that folder
# BevWiring.py, SensorNumbersMC.py and the rest all fail at import. The Data/
# tree has to be supplied separately -- from iCloud, a shared drive, or however
# it is distributed.
#
# This has bitten before, which is why it is spelled out. Data/ was previously
# ignored wholesale, that broke clones, and it was narrowed to track the inputs.
# It is now deliberately ignored wholesale again -- the reason is distribution,
# not size, and the trade-off is accepted knowingly.
#
# .gitignore DOES NOT UNTRACK WHAT GIT ALREADY TRACKS. Files committed before
# this rule stay in the repository and in its history until removed with:
#     git rm -r --cached Data
# and note that removing them from the index does not remove them from history.
Data/

# Large generated outputs, wherever they land
**/outputs/
**/raw_data/
**/histograms/

### SYSTEM FILES
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

### POSITRON / JUPYTER
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.positron/
# Monte Carlo raw draws: regenerable, large, and synced by iCloud.
*.npy

# Monte Carlo raw-draw sidecars: regenerable, written beside the .npy files.
#
# MATCHED BY FOLDER ROLE, NOT BY MODEL-FOLDER NAME. These used to read
# "PCBAreaMC/raw_data/*.json" and so on, and silently stopped matching the day
# the model folders were renumbered (2026-08-13). A rename must not be able to
# break the ignore rules -- same rule as everywhere else: a change of naming or
# composition should not change the structure.
**/raw_data/*.json
**/samples_csv/*.json
**/materials_samples_csv/*.json

# The combined composition file used to be force-tracked here as a DELIVERABLE.
# It is not tracked any more: it lives under Data/, and no data file goes to
# GitHub (see the Data/ rule above). It is handed to the stock-and-flow model
# directly, not through the repository.
#
# A negation would not work anyway. Git cannot re-include a file once its parent
# directory is excluded, so "!Data/30_..." under "Data/" is silently inert --
# a trap worth knowing about rather than rediscovering.

# Monte Carlo bulk tables are pandas pickles where they used to be CSV. Same rule
# as *.csv and *.npy above: regenerable by re-running the model, large, not source.
# 05_PCBElementMC/data_results alone is 1.7 GB.
*.pkl

# Per-draw arrays for the stock-and-flow model. Covered by *.npy above; named
# here so it is obvious they are deliberately untracked and regenerable by
# re-running tools/mc_composition.py. ~600 MB.
Composition/draws/

# Element-name sidecars written beside the .npy fraction/mass arrays. Regenerable
# with them, and meaningless without them, so they follow the same rule.
Composition/element_draws/*.txt
